    "https://www.greensboro.edu/employment/assistant-wrestling-coach/": {
      "title": "Assistant Wrestling Coach",
      "description": "Assistant Wrestling Coach | Greensboro College Skip to content Visit the Campus About GC Alumni Give To GC Translate Arabic Chinese (Simplified) Dutch English French German Italian Portuguese Russian Spanish Greensboro College Academics Admissions Financial Aid Student Life Athletics Search Menu Home » Employment » Assistant Wrestling Coach Assistant Wrestling Coach JOB SUMMARY: Greensboro College Wrestling seeks a motivated, dedicated Assistant Wrestling Coach to support the continued growth and success of our NCAA Division III wrestling programs. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Coaching and Student-Athlete Development (40%) Assist in planning and conducting daily practices. Provide technical instruction and individual skill development. Help prepare student-athletes for dual meets and tournaments. Assist with match-day coaching and competition management. Support strength and conditioning initiatives, as directed. Recruiting (30%) Assist in identifying and evaluating prospective student-athletes. Maintain recruiting communications with prospects, parents, and coaches. Attend high school tournaments and recruiting events. Assist with campus visits and recruiting days. Manage assigned recruiting territories. Academic and Student Support (15%) Monitor academic progress and class attendance. Assist with study hall and academic accountability initiatives. Support student-athlete personal development and campus involvement. Operations and Administration (15%) Assist with team travel logistics. Support equipment management and inventory. Manage team rosters and competition entries through TrackWrestling. Coordinate weigh-in procedures and event administration using TrackWrestling. Maintain accurate season records and statistics. Utilize FloWrestling and other scouting resources for opponent analysis. Assist with video breakdown and technical analysis for individual student-athletes. Create and maintain match film archives for student-athlete development and recruiting purposes. Assist with fundraising and community engagement activities. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: Bachelor’s degree required. Strong communication and organizational skills. Valid driver’s license required. Current CPR/First Aid or the ability to be certified within 14 days required. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Previous collegiate wrestling experience preferred. Previous coaching experience preferred. Familiarity with TrackWrestling tournament management software preferred. Familiarity with FloWrestling and video analysis tools preferred. Desire to pursue collegiate coaching and student-athlete development. Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) or ability to obtain one preferred. Experience operating passenger vans, buses, or towing equipment trailers preferred. To apply for this job please visit www.paycomonline.net . Create Your Path of Discovery Today Apply Visit Request Info 815 W. Market Street Greensboro, NC 27401 336.272.7102 Facebook Instagram Twitter YouTube LinkedIn Campus Conduct Hotline Conferences & Events Contact Us Employment Pride Page IT Resources Faculty / Staff Intranet Library Moodle Pride Shop Online Store Privacy Policy Registrar / Request Transcript Safety and Security See All Events Sexual Harassment Sitemap Student Sharepoint If you have difficulty accessing information on the site due to a disability or other issues, please contact: webmaster@greensboro.edu Copyright © 2026 Greensboro College | All rights reserved. Close Menu Close Menu Academics Undergraduate Degree Requirements Full Course Catalog School of the Arts Department of Theatre Audition Information Theatre Facilities Past Productions Theatre Scholarships Department of Music Ensembles Department of Art Performance Calendar School of Business Department of Business Administration & Economics Department of Accounting School of Humanities Department of English, Communication & Media Studies Department of History Department of Religion, Ethics & Philosophy School of Sciences