    "https://www.greensboro.edu/?post_type=job_listing&p=29031": {
      "title": "Security Officer",
      "description": "Security Officer  | Greensboro College Skip to content Visit the Campus About GC Alumni Give To GC Translate Arabic Chinese (Simplified) Dutch English French German Italian Portuguese Russian Spanish Greensboro College Academics Admissions Financial Aid Student Life Athletics Search Menu Home » Employment » Security Officer Security Officer Full-time JOB SUMMARY: The Security Officer is responsible for the safety and security of the college community. Responsible for enforcing the college rules, parking and traffic regulations, and providing other security and safety related services. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Advices, directs and provides information to students, employees and the public Patrols designated areas by foot, golf cart and vehicle. Patrols campus including buildings, grounds, parking lots and adjacent streets; sees that doors and windows are properly secured and locked; safeguards property of the campus. Assumes fixed post assignments. Responds to calls for service and assistance Opens and closes facilities. Monitors alarm systems and responds when necessary. Monitors and controls access to building and restricted areas Inspects building for security, fire, and potential accident and/or hazards and takes preventive or corrective action as appropriate Provides escort services by foot and/or vehicle Provides security for large gatherings such as football, basketball, soccer, high school graduations and college commencement activities Complete first aid and CPR training along with operating an AED Makes preliminary investigation of crimes and disorders along with conducting searches within the scope of employment Enforces vehicle parking regulations Carries mace/pepper spray and handcuffs Enforces rules and regulations of the College while cooperating with other police agencies Additional duties as assigned SKILLS AND QUALIFICATIONS: High school diploma or equivalent and 21 years of age A minimum of one year of related work experience, preferably in an institutional or campus environment, but will train Must have a valid driver’s license Good customer relations skills and the ability to communicate clearly; ability to think and act quickly and effectively in emergencies; ability to analyze situations accurately and make appropriate decisions Intermediate proficiency in Word, Excel, and other officer related skills Good report writing skills Physical Requirements Heavy lifting, carrying, pushing and pulling up to 130 pounds Bending, stretching, and reaching required Some sitting, running and climbing, extensive walking and standing Rarely but possible working in extreme temperatures, wet, humid, and hot Physical ability to restrain individuals Physical ability to intervene in altercations on campus To apply for this job please visit www.paycomonline.net . Create Your Path of Discovery Today Apply Visit Request Info 815 W. Market Street Greensboro, NC 27401 336.272.7102 Facebook Instagram Twitter YouTube LinkedIn Campus Conduct Hotline Conferences & Events Contact Us Employment Pride Page IT Resources Faculty / Staff Intranet Library Moodle Pride Shop Online Store Privacy Policy Registrar / Request Transcript Safety and Security See All Events Sexual Harassment Sitemap Student Sharepoint If you have difficulty accessing information on the site due to a disability or other issues, please contact: webmaster@greensboro.edu Copyright © 2026 Greensboro College | All rights reserved. Close Menu Close Menu Academics Admissions Financial Aid Student Life Athletics About Greensboro College Library Visit the Campus Give To GC Alumni Current Students Faculty & Staff Resources IT Resources Parents Employment Events News Contact Us Academics Undergraduate Degree Requirements Full Course Catalog School of the Arts School of Business School of Humanities School of Sciences & Mathematics School of Social Sciences & Education Graduate Programs Educator Preparation Program International Programs & Study Abroad S